  "methodology": [
    "Reran only the largest post-refinement regressions (Door, AstroVision, Gerrard Hall, Palace) and Skydio-32 (pose regression and legacy crash).",
    "New runs use the production RootSIFTDetectorDescriptor. Legacy RootSIFT is an experiment-only adapter copied from the prior comparison, with its original float32 output cast.",
    "Every trial preserves the previous loader, resolution, retrieval, matching, verifier, and backend settings except the two implementation fixes. Same rank-three Shonan without certification for Gerrard Hall and Palace.",
    "Each run executes the complete pipeline, including global 2D track assembly, first BA, actual retriangulation, final BA and filtering. No COLMAP feature extractor or VLFeat was run.",
    "Full-reference relative-pose AUC uses max(rotation error, translation-direction error) for every reference-image pair, counting missing cameras as failures. Percentages are absolute AUC values.",
    "These are single-run comparisons; first-BA geometry can have small numerical/run-to-run differences. The earlier BA-only ablations additionally isolate the effect on identical saved input.",
    "All selected benchmarks use SinglePartitioner. They test final retriangulation/refinement; actual multi-cluster merging is covered by the regression test, not a multi-cluster dataset rerun.",
    "The stock dashboard shows unmodified pipeline metrics and uncontrolled runtime. Use full-reference-comparison.json for a consistent reference-image denominator."
  ],
